# places-india.db (~97MB) is already committed to this repo, as a one-time
# addition (per explicit request). It stays tracked, but should NOT be
# recommitted/replaced on routine pushes — every regular commit to this repo
# should only ever touch the small places.db plus code changes, never
# re-add or modify places-india.db. If you genuinely need to rebuild it
# (e.g. GeoNames publishes an update), that's a deliberate one-off: rebuild
# it with import-geonames.js, review the diff, and commit it by itself with
# a clear message — don't let it ride along with unrelated commits.
node_modules/
